class_name LevelConfig
extends RefCounted

## Data for the test level that character_switcher.gd builds in code (the level
## scene stays minimal because the editor keeps clobbering it). Move these into a
## real level scene's inspector when the dev harness is retired.
##
## This is a VERTICAL level: a tall zigzag tower you climb from the ground floor up.
## The camera follows the player (character_switcher._physics_process), so there is no
## height limit -- add more PLATFORMS rows to build higher. Steps are ~70-95px apart,
## staggered left/right, so each is one jump + an air-jump from the one below.

## Player start on the ground floor, left of the tower base so you spawn in the clear.
## Also the respawn point on death / falling out.
const SPAWN := Vector2(-450, 0)
## Fall below this (well under the ground floor) and you respawn instead of dropping
## forever. The floor sits at y~0, so falling off the tower drops you back to it, not
## to death -- you only respawn if you leave the world past the floor's edges.
const DEATH_Y := 300.0

## Jump-up platforms, each [center_x, top_y, width]. A rising zigzag tower: the player
## climbs ground -> P1 -> P2 -> ... using the jump + generous air jumps. One-way, so you
## jump up through each and land on top (press down+jump to drop back through).
## Add/remove rows to change the height; keep steps within ~100px of the row below.
